  "note": "Election of 12 members for the two wards of Warrenpoint Urban District on 17 May 1961: East Ward 5 seats, West Ward 7. The five Unionist members for East Ward were returned unopposed; West Ward was contested. Fourteen candidates contested the ward; the 'How they fared' table prints all fourteen with their votes (the seven defeated by surname; the first names of the four defeated outgoing councillors, P. Finnison, G. McKevitt, Ed. McNeill and Patrick O'Neill, are given in the text). Only two outgoing councillors, Fay and McGreevy, were re-elected.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Newry Telegraph, 20 May 1961, p. 8 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the seven defeated candidates printed with their votes in the 'How they fared' table were added (Fitzpatrick 225, McKevitt 222, O'Neill 212, Finnison 204, McNeill 198, Caulfield 175, Moore 171). Corrected from the page image of Newry Telegraph, 20 May 1961, p. 8 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the seven candidates printed 'Eire Labour' / '(E.L.)' had no Party_Name; set to Irish Labour (the paper's 'Eire Labour' is the Irish Labour Party, whose 1958 Warrenpoint candidates these are), Party_As_Printed kept as printed."
